# Angular Material UI (Vuetify port)

This project uses **Angular Material only** for UI. The Vue reference app uses Vuetify.

When porting a Vue screen:

1. Read the Vue template for **structure and behaviour** (what the user can do).
2. Replace each Vuetify tag with the **closest Material component** (button → `mat-button`, card → `mat-card`, grid → CSS grid, dialog → `MatDialog`, etc.).
3. Use **default Material styling** — no copying Vuetify colors, SCSS, or pixel-perfect layout.
4. Avoid feature-level `.scss` unless a Material component cannot express the layout.

Full conventions: `docs/angular-frontend-development-plan.md` §8.

## Routing

- **`APPS_MANAGER_ROUTES` must be first** in `app.routes.ts` — other apps use `path: ''` and will steal `/` if registered earlier.

## Buttons (global)

- **Shape:** `4px` border radius — `mat.button-overrides` / `mat.icon-button-overrides` in `src/styles.scss`. **Never** pill shapes (`999px`).
- **Paired actions:** secondary = `mat-stroked-button`, primary = `mat-flat-button color="primary"`, row with `justify-content: space-between` + `gap: 12px`. **Never** two `mat-flat-button` (accent + primary look identical in Material 22).
- **Dialog / auth forms:** same stroked + flat pattern; use `div.form-actions`, not two flat buttons in `mat-card-actions`.

## Cards & grids

- **Card shape:** `mat.card-overrides` **8px** radius in `styles.scss`.
- **Images:** `aspect-ratio: 3 / 2` + `object-fit: cover` + `width: 100%`. **Never** `height="200" width="100%"` without `object-fit` — images stretch.
- **Equal height in grid:** `:host { height: 100% }`, card `display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%`, actions `margin-top: auto`.
- **Text truncation:** product cards — title `line-clamp: 1`, description `line-clamp: 2`.
- **Card actions:** prefer `div.card-actions` with `justify-content: space-between` — `mat-card-actions` can break spacing.
- **Grids:** CSS `display: grid` responsive 1/2/3 cols, `max-width: 1600px`. **No** `mat-grid-list` with fixed `rowHeight`.

## Layout shells

- **Feature layouts:** `min-height: 100vh`, column flex; `main { flex: 1 }` so footer sits at bottom.
- **Auth / status pages:** `AuthPageShellComponent` — vertical + horizontal center. Page `:host { flex: 1; width: 100% }`.
- **Product detail:** same centering pattern as auth pages.
- **Form width:** `max-width` on form component `:host`, **not** `display: flex` on `<form>` (shrinks card).
- **Field spacing:** `margin-bottom: 12px` on fields; `padding-top: 12px` on `mat-card-content` below title.

## Tables, dividers, cart

- Table / card horizontal padding **24px**; `mat-card-actions` `8px 24px 24px`.
- `mat-divider` in wrapper with same horizontal inset as table (`.section-divider { padding: 0 24px }`).
- Table row components: `selector: 'tr[app-*]'` with `<td>` only — no host breaking `<tbody>`.

## Snackbars

- `panelClass: app-message-{error|success|warning}` with **container** background colors in `styles.scss` (not button color only).

## Dialogs & a11y

- Search dialogs: `panelClass` + `8px` radius on `.mat-mdc-dialog-surface` in `styles.scss`.
- **No** HTML `autofocus` in templates — use `MatDialog.open({ autoFocus: 'first-toggler' })`.

## Animations

- **No** `provideAnimationsAsync()` / `provideAnimations()` in `app.config.ts` — deprecated; Material MDC uses CSS.

## Apps Manager (Phase 2 patterns)

- Hero: tall banner, `public/bg-*.jpg`, parallax (`background-attachment: fixed`), centered title.
- Navbar: actions right; **All Apps** menu; no duplicate title button; icon+label gap on trigger.
- Grid `max-width: 1600px`; footer three-column layout.

## Angular templates

- Signals in templates: `signal()` with parentheses.
- `mat-card-subtitle`: avoid `@if` projection traps — split branches per card.
- Check angular.dev / Context7 before adding deprecated providers (`provideAnimations*`).

## Infrastructure

- No Docker — `npm start` locally, Firebase Hosting for deploy.
- Static images in `public/`.

## Testing

- Every new **component** needs `.component.spec.ts` (create + key states/behaviour).
- API services and stores: HTTP + state tests mandatory.
